WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:01.601 line:0%
And finally...

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:05.471 line:0%
New rule, someone has to
convince President Biden

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:07.006 line:0%
that if he runs again,

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:09.909 line:0%
he's going to turn the country
back over to Trump,

00:00:10.242 --> 00:00:11.343 line:0%
-and go--
-(SOFT CLAPPING)

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.479 line:0%
-(LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:17.183 line:0%
And go down in history
as Ruth Bader Biden.

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:18.984 line:0%
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:21.220 line:0%
The person who doesn't know
when to quit,

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:24.390 line:0%
and so does great damage to
their party and their country.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:27.193 line:0%
All of us who like Joe Biden
have been struggling lately

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.995
with the political situation
of the Democratic Party.

00:00:30.195 --> 00:00:31.697
An incumbent we admire,

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.833
who acquitted himself well
in a first term,

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:35.635
but who even members
of his own party

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.436
don't want to see run
for a second.

00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:39.905
Despite a touching letter
of recommendation

00:00:40.005 --> 00:00:41.774
from Ashton Kutcher
and Mila Kunis.

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:44.344
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.812
I kid. They shouldn't
have gotten shit for that.

00:00:47.012 --> 00:00:48.981
If you ask me
do I think Joe Biden

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:50.850
can do the job of president,

00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:54.553
my answer is an unequivocal
"Yes, he can do the job."

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.091
Do I love everything, no.
But that's every president.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:01.560
But government work is done
in small, quiet rooms

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.796
like the Oval Office,
and in that setting,

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:06.966
Joe's compassion
and centuries of experience...

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:10.570
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.238
...are pluses.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:14.006
And he's generally made
good decisions

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:17.043
that got us out of Afghanistan,
handled Ukraine,

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.645
kept the economy chugging,

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.980
finally got us rebuilding
infrastructure,

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.882
returned a sense of normalcy.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:26.186
There's a term for Joe Biden.
But not two.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:33.159
(LAUGHTER, APPLAUSE)

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:40.300
Because while he can do the job,
what he can't do is run for it.

00:01:40.966 --> 00:01:42.969
Our campaign season is long,

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.437
and it gets icy
in New Hampshire.

00:01:45.337 --> 00:01:48.475
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:52.411
To those who say he beat
Trump once, he'll do it again,

00:01:52.544 --> 00:01:54.547
I say, things change.

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:57.182
They always do.
The parade moves on.

00:01:57.549 --> 00:02:01.187
2024 is not 2020
in so many key ways,

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.657
including, yes,
Biden being four years older.

00:02:05.924 --> 00:02:07.360
You can be a national treasure

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.362
and still be
too old for the job.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.164
If I'm on a plane
and the pilot says,

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.499
"This is your captain,
Buzz Aldrin..."

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:16.236
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)
-...I'm getting off.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:23.209
(APPLAUSE)

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:27.980
Mitch McConnell
has served Satan well.

00:02:28.247 --> 00:02:32.218
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:36.455
But when he starts buffering
during a speech...

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:40.960
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:44.497
...and it appears his soul
is leaving his body...

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:51.538
(LAUGHTER, APPLAUSE)

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.011
...it's time.

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:00.913
I have made it a theme
on this show

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:02.749
to rail against ageism,

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:05.318
the last acceptable prejudice
in America.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:08.988
I've tried to make the argument
that judging by age is wrong

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:11.423
because we all age
so differently.

00:03:11.523 --> 00:03:13.860
Some people are old
when they're 45,

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.728
and others are spry at 90.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:18.697
So it should always be
a case-by-case basis.

00:03:18.897 --> 00:03:21.967
But the credibility
of my argument against ageism

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:25.838
rests on the honest calling out
of people when it is time to go.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.907
That's what
"case by case" means.

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:31.644
At an event last weekend,
Biden referred to LL Cool J

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.479
as LL J Cool J.

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:36.082
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:40.286
Say what you want about Trump,
but he remembers Kanye's name.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:45.658
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:50.096
Look, at some point,
perception becomes reality.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:53.299
What matters is voters think
Biden's too old.

00:03:53.432 --> 00:03:56.669
What matters is
he's gonna lose to Trump,

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:57.837
who's almost the same age,

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:00.239
but his age just doesn't
read like Biden's.

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:02.108
Maybe it's because
Trump is insane,

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:04.877
maybe it's because he's always
a ball of white-hot anger,

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:07.313
but for whatever reason,
he looks robust,

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:10.483
and Joe looks like
his own skeletal remains.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:14.921
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:04:16.388 --> 00:04:20.727
If this was 1860,
when Joe first ran...

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:23.763
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:04:24.429 --> 00:04:26.165
...this would not be an issue.

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:27.900
You didn't have to look good,

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:29.501
and there was no
ubiquitous media

00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:31.470
to pick on every little mistake.

00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:34.506
The only people who saw
the Lincoln-Douglas debates

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.108
were the people
who went to them.

00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:39.411
But Joe's debates next year
will be televised to all,

00:04:39.511 --> 00:04:41.480
and I don't think
he's gonna look good.

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:44.149
Yes, Trump is old too,
but Trump is like KISS.

00:04:44.249 --> 00:04:46.119
He puts on the face paint
and the wig...

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:49.188
(LAUGHTER, APPLAUSE)

00:04:49.321 --> 00:04:52.358
...and he looks the same
as he did in 1978.

00:04:55.394 --> 00:04:59.098
Far from being the only one
who could beat Trump in 2024,

00:04:59.231 --> 00:05:02.167
Biden may well be the only
Democrat who would lose to him.

00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:04.003
James Carville told me

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:06.339
any centers Democrat
around 50 or 60

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:08.073
would get 55 percent
of the vote,

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:09.274
and I believe him.

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:12.545
You know that
Future Headlines bit we do?

00:05:12.778 --> 00:05:15.747
Well, the most predictable
headline ever is,

00:05:15.814 --> 00:05:17.749
"Presidential Race Tied."

00:05:18.517 --> 00:05:20.653
Two weeks before every election,
it's always tied,

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:22.087
no matter who is running.

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:25.324
The vast majority just vote
for the D or the R.

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:27.326
But Biden is the one Democrat

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:29.061
who gives pause
to so many people,

00:05:29.161 --> 00:05:30.663
even in his own party.

00:05:31.263 --> 00:05:33.199
Andrew Sullivan
makes the necessary point

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:35.001
that a new nominee
for the Democrats

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:37.102
would shift
the dynamic immediately.

00:05:37.369 --> 00:05:41.073
Trump would be the tired old guy
retread hanging onto the past,

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:43.309
and the Democrat
would now be the future.

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:45.845
Let the Republicans be
the party with the candidate

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:48.247
who babbles nonsense,
shouts at the TV,

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:49.582
and can't do ramps.

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:56.255
(LAUGHTER, APPLAUSE)

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:01.894
Joe, you did noble service
for your country,

00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:03.595
and you checked that big box,

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:05.898
the President
of the United States.

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:08.834
Of course, as a politician,
you're naturally gonna say,

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:12.505
"But the work is not finished."
Of course not, it never is.

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:15.307
But it's time to let
someone else finish it.

00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:20.146
You don't want to go down
as Ruth Bader Biden.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.882
America is calling, Joe,
and it's saying,

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:26.386
"That's not our car, grandpa,
we're over here."

